    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d692">

                <pb facs="0902" n="892" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg892"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/10–1147: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-10-11T13:00:00+09:00">October 11, 1947—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 11—7:27 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2060. Following for President Truman from Representatives Cole,<anchor n="64"
                        xml:id="d692-f1"/> Hébert,<anchor n="65" xml:id="d692-f2"/> Hess<anchor
                        n="66" xml:id="d692-f3"/> and Norblad,<anchor n="67" xml:id="d692-f4"/>
                    Members Armed Services Committee, House of Representatives.</p>
                <p>A considered survey of Chinese-American interests prompts us to urge extension of
                    immediate aid to the Chinese Government by meeting its appropriate needs from
                    our available military materials and reviving implementation of previous
                    commitments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
